      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "मुखानि येषां तैः but the text is not दीनातिदीन &c. which would spoil",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the metre; दीना in truth goes with गेहिनी and दीनमुखैः with शिशुकैः.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "नरैः the commentator explains by अन्यैश्च गृहनरैः which is not correct.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "नरैः answers to the जनः in the last line. “If men did not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "see... what man of strong mind &c.” त्रुट्यत् = broken हृदिस्थाभिप्राया-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "दन्यत्क (sic) थनेन भग्नतां प्राप्तवत्. (commentary). विलीन = lost in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "articulation, not distinctly pronounced. The whole is an adverbial",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "compound. दग्ध = क्षुधातापेनाकुल. (Râmarshi). But comp. note, Nîti-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "s'ataka St. 94, also Kâdambarî p. 326. Uttararâmacharita p. 95",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "and 156.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. IX.—पुरुषबहुमानः = Râmarshi says पुरुषसंबन्धी पुरुषाणां यूनां यो भव-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "तीत्यर्थः स बहुमानो भूरिरहंकारः स विगलितः भ्रष्टः वृद्धो हि निरहंकारं वक्ति",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "कर्म करोतीत्यर्थः. The other commentary explains it to mean respect",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "among men, which I think better. The alternative of taking",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "पुरुष as a vocative I do not think a good one. The commentary",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "comments on जीवितसमाः thus जीवितं समं पूर्णं येषां अथवा जीवनतुल्यास्ते दुर्हृद-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "स्तिष्ठन्तु म्रियन्तां वा तैः किमित्यर्थः. Whence this last portion comes",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "does not appear; for सम meaning पूर्ण there is no authority that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "I am aware of, and there is also a further difficulty, but not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "quite insuperable, about the position of सम in the com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "pound. Râmarshi has प्राणतुल्याः simply, which is correct. Râmar-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "shi supplies स्वर्याताः with सुहृदः and thus makes the line consist of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "two statements. It would be better I think to take it as one",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "statement. समाना जीवितसमाः सुहृदः सपदि स्वर्याताः. धृष्टः Râmarshi renders",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "by निर्लज्ज which is appropriate. But one of the other readings",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "would perhaps be preferable, as the meaning of निर्लज्ज can only",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "be got by some straining, and the ordinary sense of “bold” will",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "not suit here.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. X.—व्यालानां मरुदशनं कल्पितम् — one of the synonymes given",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "by Amara of सर्प is पवनाशनः. वृत्तिः = mode of living. Comp. St. 59",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
